---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
export const prerender = false;
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy | After Hours Outreach Initiative"
  description="Draft privacy information for volunteer accounts and events."
  noindex
  privatePage
>
  <section class="bg-black px-6 py-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <h1 class="text-blue">Privacy</h1>
      <p
        class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-amber-800 bg-amber-950/30 p-5 text-amber-200"
      >
        {
          import.meta.env.DEV
            ? "This is local development, not the final privacy policy. Use sample information only. Accounts, profiles, and events are saved in local D1 on this computer. No real emails are sent."
            : "This privacy policy is still being reviewed. Use sample profile answers until the policy is finalized."
        }
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-12">Your information</h2>
      <p class="mt-6">
        {
          import.meta.env.DEV
            ? "Your email identifies your local account. Sign-in emails are shown in a development dialog instead of sent. Profile answers are stored in local D1, not browser storage. Sessions use an HttpOnly cookie. The development View as buttons can switch to any user in the local database without an email or authenticator challenge."
            : "Your email identifies your account and receives sign-in emails through Resend. Profile answers are saved in Cloudflare D1 in the US. Date of birth is used for age and eligibility; emergency contacts and optional medical information help support volunteer safety. Profile edits are logged by field name, without copying your answers. Sessions use a necessary HttpOnly cookie; profile answers are not saved in browser storage."
        }
        The Code of Conduct version and the time you acknowledge it are saved with
        your profile to record your registration confirmation.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-12">Organizer access and events</h2>
      <p class="mt-6">
        Active, registered organizers can manage volunteers and view full
        profiles. Two-factor authentication is optional; accounts that enable it
        must use it when signing in. Full profile views and edits are logged;
        audit entries do not copy sensitive answers. Event rosters contain
        volunteer names, not medical or emergency-contact answers. Event
        registrations, attendance, access decisions, cancellations, and
        notification records are saved in D1. {
          import.meta.env.DEV
            ? "Notification delivery is simulated locally."
            : "Event and access changes send notifications through Resend."
        }
        Do not include sensitive personal information in an organizer’s emailed reason.
        Cancelled event and registration records are retained while retention rules
        are reviewed.
      </p>
      <h2 class="mt-12">Before launch</h2>
      <p class="mt-6">
        The privacy contact, retention and deletion policy, and handling of
        sensitive information still need review before collecting real volunteer
        data.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
